Too slow, too risky.  Nethack is a game of minimizing risk.  Running
around the Mines (potentially dark!) with low HP and hiding behind your
pet is obviously more risky than running around those same Mines with
that same pet, except levelled up to get more HP, more to-hit, etc. etc.

Nethack is also a game where the most dangerous part for any character
is the early game.  The protection racket advocates making the early
game more risky in order to make the mid- and late-game (which aren't
much of a risk at all) even less so.  This is backwards thought;
optimizing play directly involves making the early game safer to
increase the probability of characters making it to the less-risky parts
of the game.

